   "lines": [
    "# Masm Debugger Clone",
    "",
    "",
    "### A console MASM-style virtual machine and debugger in C++ for stepping through assembly and inspecting CPU state.",
    "",
    "A console-based virtual machine emulator inspired by vintage emulators,",
    "built to show how a processor handles tasks at a low level. It simulates a",
    "simplified CPU with customizable registers and flags, supports hex-dump",
    "memory views with editing, assembly input and execution, step-by-step",
    "tracing with real-time register updates, and debugging aids such as",
    "breakpoints and memory watches. A command shell (dump, enter, fill, move,",
    "search, assemble, unassemble, trace) drives it, and instructions persist to",
    "memory.txt. Designed for education and system-level debugging, and released",
    "under the MIT License.",
    "",
    "Built with C++ · MSVC · Git · CPU emulation",
    "",
    "[Visit](https://github.com/Usman-Khalil/Masm_Debugger_Project)",
    "[README](https://github.com/Usman-Khalil/Masm_Debugger_Project#readme)"
   ]
